  "schemaVersion": "1.0",
  "scriptId": "bs-03-round-trips-average-speed",
  "sourceType": "MANUAL",
  "metadata": {
    "title": "Round Trips, Total Time, and Average Speed",
    "description": "Add upstream and downstream times correctly, recover distance, and find whole-trip average speed.",
    "teachingApproach": "Start with a short out-and-back trip and keep each leg visible. Show why total time is a sum and why average speed must use total distance divided by total time. Then reverse the setup to find distance, still-water speed, current, and partial-return distances.",
    "targetDurationMinutes": 30,
    "sourceScope": "R.S. Aggarwal, Quantitative Aptitude for Competitive Examinations, Chapter 19, Boats and Streams. Approved scope: Teach an upstream-downstream round trip as two equal-distance legs with different effective speeds. Cover finding the one-way distance from total time, finding total time from a known distance, equal-distance average speed using total distance divided by total time, comparing a boat round trip with a road traveller, partial returns such as coming back to a midpoint, and reverse problems where total round-trip time plus current speed determines still-water speed. Include the chapter pattern where a boat of known still-water speed travels a fixed distance downstream and back in a given total time, leading to a simple quadratic that factors cleanly."
  },
  "startNodeId": "start",
  "nodes": {
    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn how a river changes a round trip.\n\nThe distance out and back may be the same, but the times are not. Treat the two legs separately, then join them at the end.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1": {
      "id": "teach_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A boat moves at 5 km/hr in still water and the current is 1 km/hr.\n\nDownstream = 6 km/hr\nUpstream = 4 km/hr.\n\nSuppose the place is x km away.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "teach_1_step"
        }
      ]
    },
    "teach_1_step": {
      "id": "teach_1_step",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "The round-trip time is:\n\nx/6 + x/4.\n\nIf the whole trip takes 1 hour:\n2x/12 + 3x/12 = 1\n5x/12 = 1\nx = 2.4 km.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "q_1": {
      "id": "q_1",
      "type": "CHOICE",
      "content": {
        "text": "A boat moves at 5 km/hr in still water, current is 1 km/hr, and an out-and-back trip takes 1 hour. How far away is the turning point?",
